# Biostatistics & Epidemiology Admission Portfolio

An applied biostatistics and epidemiology portfolio demonstrating statistical analysis, epidemiological modelling, data visualization, and time-series forecasting using Python.

## Features

- Epidemiological data analysis
- Descriptive statistics
- Hypothesis testing
- Logistic regression
- Risk-factor analysis
- Interactive visualizations
- SIR infectious disease modelling
- Time-series forecasting
- Streamlit interactive dashboard

## Technologies

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- SciPy
- Statsmodels
- Scikit-learn
- Plotly
- Streamlit

## Project Purpose

This project was developed as an academic portfolio to demonstrate quantitative reasoning, statistical programming, epidemiological analysis, and computational modelling relevant to biostatistics and epidemiology.

## Important Note

The demonstration dataset used by this application is synthetic and is intended for educational and portfolio purposes only. It does not represent real clinical or public-health data.

## Run Locally

Install the required packages:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
